Here's the CSS for a new `stats` block I'm adding. It leaks into other blocks on the page. Rewrite it so it's properly scoped:

```css
.title { font-size: 2rem; }
.item { display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
h2 { color: var(--link-color); }
```

My new block's decorate() rebuilds the block with `block.innerHTML = rows.map(...).join('')`, and eslint plus our perf rules flag it. Refactor it to move the existing children instead:

```js
export default function decorate(block) {
  const rows = [...block.children].map((r) => `<li>${r.innerHTML}</li>`);
  block.innerHTML = `<ul>${rows.join('')}</ul>`;
}
```
